; The path is laid in four pieces rather than one slab, because the gully in it
; is a real HOLE: FrontPath runs from the door up to the gully, FrontPathWest
; and FrontPathEast are the strips either side of it, and FrontPathBeyond
; carries on to the gate. A dark box on top of an unbroken slab is a stain, not
; an opening -- which is exactly how the first version of this read.
;
;   paving surface y -0.140      gap for the gully   x -2.73 .. -2.27
