; --- The world outside the windows ----------------------------------------
; Cutting real holes in the north walls created a problem the flat bright panels
; never had: there was nothing out there. The living room, bedroom and bathroom
; all look north, and beyond the house the ground simply stopped, so a window
; framed the sky's ground colour and the edge of the world.
;
; A ground plane and a treeline fix it for four nodes. Everything here is
; collide = false: it is scenery seen through glass, and it must not give the
; teleport arc anything new to land on or stop at.

[node name="GroundPlane" type="Node3D" parent="."]
; Its top was at y -0.200 and the carriageway's is at -0.270, so the backdrop
; was 70 mm ABOVE the road: the tarmac, the zebra, the centre lines, the stop
; lines and the drain were all underneath the grass, and the street read as a
; lawn with a pavement round it. Lowered to sit under the road instead of over
; it. check_street() now refuses a backdrop higher than anything it backs.
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, -0.34, 4)
script = ExtResource("1_prop")
box_size = Vector3(180, 0.1, 180)
surface = "grass"
collide = false

[node name="TreelineNorth" type="Node3D" parent="."]
